<title>MOROCCO: Euro-Mediterranean business summit set for Dec 5.</title>
<headline>Euro-Mediterranean business summit set for Dec 5.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Businessmen and officials from 27 countries in Europe and the Middle East are to attend a Euro- Mediterranean summit of company leaders in Morocco on December 5 and 6, organisers said on Monday.</p>
<p>The Moroccan General Confederation of Business, which is organising the event in the city of Marrakesh, said that among European countries represented would be Britain, Belgium, France, Germany, Sweden, and Spain.</p>
<p>Egyptian, Israeli, Jordanian, Lebanese, Palestinian and Syrian business leaders or government officials would also be attending, it added.</p>
<p>Topics include multilateral industrial cooperation across the Mediterranean, the European Union's policy for the region, integration of the economies of south Mediterranean countries, tourism and the environment.</p>
</text>
